at last year's showcase I told you about  the Elder Scrolls legends a free-to-play  collectible card game now as I said last  year I am a huge fans of these games I  play them a lot so this is a game I'm  particularly excited about legends  provides a very deep strategy experience  through both single and multiplayer  modes beginning with the campaign  complete with a compelling story  interesting characters and some great  gameplay the story is told from the  perspective of a moth priest named  Kellan I'll let him tell you a little  more as we take a look at the campaigns  opening cinematic  the elder scrolls show us what was  and what he had hoobae  and they have revealed much to me spare  us your stories old man unless they can  sharpen Spears our war chief is dying  our enemies are massing for another  attack we must prepare for battle we  should kill him we have this growl we  came for and this one smells blood in  the wind patience knock I have words yet  to speak hear stories can do surprising  things spear maidens  this is the story of a forgotten hero  who changed the very course of history  when Legends begins you're set on a path  to discover the world of the Elder  Scrolls in a way you haven't seen before  the choices you make to find your  approach and unlock all the depth the  game has to offer a two-lane battlefield  provides more variety and strategic  depth players make decisions that change  the cards they want to improve or add to  their decks and we offer full  single-player campaign as well as  multiple ways to play against the AI or  other players in both battle and arena  modes now we began public beta testing  in April and so far the feedback from  the people who have been playing has  been terrific to celebrate III this week  we'll be letting even more of you into  the beta to start playing now if you  haven't signed up yet  just visit bethesda net create an  account and sign up and be sure to keep  an eye on your email also tonight we're  very pleased to announce that in  addition to PC and iPad legends we'll be  coming to iPhone Mac and Android tablets  and phones later this year  as I said I'm very excited about legends  as it brings together an award-winning  franchise that I love and a new genre  and whether you're a veteran strategy  card fan or have never played a game  before it's a game we think you'll all  really enjoy
 

